        "title": "An Extraordinary Experience!!",
        "text": "The Pashupatinath Temple is one of the structures that withstood the earthquake. My guide toured me around the area....it's a huge place that is spread out between the sacred Bhagmati river, Unexpectedly there was a couple of cremation services that was going on....seemed to be a normal process that I found people around were just comfortable watching this holy ceremony, the family members of the deceased and the visitors /tourists like me. This is a Hindu Sacred Temple so only the faithful are admitted and on the opposite of the river is the place for others to watch. \nAside from the on going ritual, one has to look around and be amazed.....Pashupatinath is a collection of beautiful stupas in different dimensions and weathered finishes and the Hindu Temple is an imposing but beautiful sight. It does not matter if you are for or against the purpose of the site....Pashupatinah is fascinating!",
