        "title": "Very colorful and very interesting ",
        "text": "This is one of the most interesting sights in Kathmandu. Extremely colorful. You will see the preparation of the bodies for cremation,  the ceremony carrying the body to the burning site  and you will see the actual burning of the bodies. There are naked sadhus walking around, there are holy men doing readings and giving blessings. There are beautiful temples, Most of them you can not enter unless you are Buddhist but just looking outside can give you a good idea. Bring your camera because wherever you look there is a photo. You can combine this with a trip to the Boudha stupa. The walk from one to the other is very interesting and takes you through some lovely temples. ",
