        "title": "Sobering experience not to be missed ",
        "text": "We want here last at the end of a long day and I'm glad we did. The atmosphere from the opposite bank to the cremation pyres is hushed, almost reverential. It's hard not to be affected especially when you see a corpse being laid out by the river ahead of the cremation. Well worth continuing over the bridge to the smaller \"VIP\" area best viewed from the top terrace. It's a bit of a climb but we'll worth it for the views down the whole river section. The monkeys provide some well needed relief. ",
